This passes an inline style object literal (`{pointerEvents: inert ? 'none' : 'box-none'}`) to a style prop. Inline objects allocate a new object every render and bypass the shared style system, which already provides equivalents for both branches (`styles.pointerEventsNone` and `styles.pointerEventsBoxNone`).

Use the existing style helpers instead:

```tsx
<View
    aria-hidden={inert}
    style={[styles.flex1, inert ? styles.pointerEventsNone : styles.pointerEventsBoxNone]}
    collapsable={false}
>
    {children}
</View>
```

This line passes an inline style object literal (`{paddingLeft}`) to a style-typed prop. Per `STYLING.md`, inline style objects are disallowed: they create a new object every render (breaking memoization) and bypass the shared style system. A `StyleUtils` helper already exists for exactly this case — `StyleUtils.getPaddingLeft(paddingLeft)` (see `src/styles/utils/index.ts`).

Use the helper instead of the inline object:

```tsx
const StyleUtils = useStyleUtils();
// ...
style={[
    styles.textLabelSupporting,
    styles.lh16,
    isAlternateTextMultilineSupported ? styles.preWrap : styles.pre,
    isAlternateTextMultilineSupported ? {maxWidth: alternateTextMaxWidth} : null,
    isMultilineSupported ? StyleUtils.getPaddingLeft(paddingLeft) : null,
]}
```

This passes an inline object literal to the `contentContainerStyle` style prop. Inline style objects create a new object every render (breaking memoization) and bypass the shared style system. A `StyleUtils` helper already exists for exactly this case.

Use `StyleUtils.getWidthStyle(scrollWidth)` instead:

```tsx
const StyleUtils = useStyleUtils();
// ...
contentContainerStyle={StyleUtils.getWidthStyle(scrollWidth)}
```

This passes an inline style object literal (`{transform: [{rotate: '180deg'}]}`) to `additionalStyles`, which is a style-typed prop (`StyleProp<ViewStyle>`). Per `STYLING.md`, inline style objects are not allowed: they allocate a new object every render (breaking memoization) and duplicate a value that already exists in the shared style system. A direct equivalent already exists as `styles.flipUpsideDown` (`transform: rotate(180deg)`).

Use the existing style token instead of an inline object:

```tsx
<Icon
    src={icons.DownArrow}
    fill={theme.icon}
    additionalStyles={isSkippedSectionExpanded ? styles.flipUpsideDown : undefined}
/>
```

Per `STYLING.md`, inline style object literals must not be passed to style-typed props. Here `{borderWidth: variables.avatarBorderWidthSmall}` is an inline object literal placed inside the `iconAdditionalStyles` style array. A `StyleUtils` helper already produces exactly this shape (`getAvatarBorderWidth` returns `{borderWidth: avatarBorderWidths[size]}`), and `CONST.AVATAR_SIZE.SMALL` maps to `avatarBorderWidthSmall`, so the shared helper can be reused instead of an ad-hoc object.

```tsx
iconAdditionalStyles={[
    // The medium subscript on a xxxx-large avatar keeps the small border width...
    size === CONST.AVATAR_SIZE.XXXX_LARGE
        ? StyleUtils.getAvatarBorderWidth(CONST.AVATAR_SIZE.SMALL)
        : StyleUtils.getAvatarBorderWidth(isSmall ? CONST.AVATAR_SIZE.XXXX_SMALL : subscriptAvatarSize),
    StyleUtils.getBorderColorStyle(subscriptAvatarBorderColor ?? theme.componentBG),
]}
```

This passes an inline style object literal `{minHeight: undefined}` to the `style` prop. Per `STYLING.md`, inline style objects are not allowed — they allocate a new object on every render (breaking memoization) and bypass the shared style system.

Add a named style helper/token that overrides `minHeight` and use it instead:

```tsx
// src/styles/index.ts
mapViewContainerNoMinHeight: {
    minHeight: undefined,
},

// index.tsx
<View style={[styles.mapViewContainer, styles.mapViewContainerNoMinHeight]}>
```

This passes an inline style object literal `{height: 64}` to the `style` prop. Per `STYLING.md`, inline style objects are not allowed — they create a new object every render (breaking memoization), bypass the theme system, and hardcode a magic pixel value (`64`) that belongs in the style system.

Move this to a named style in `src/styles/index.ts` (alongside the sibling `sliderBar`/`editStopSliderFilled` styles you already added) and use a named variable for the height instead of the literal `64`:

```tsx
// src/styles/index.ts
editStopSliderContainer: {
    height: variables.editStopSliderContainerHeight,
    ...
},

// Slider.tsx
<View style={[styles.editStopSliderContainer, styles.ph5, styles.justifyContentCenter]}>
```

Inline style object literals are not allowed per `STYLING.md`. This container recreates a circular-avatar style on every render (`width`/`height`/`borderRadius`/`overflow`), bypassing the shared style system. An equivalent already exists: `StyleUtils.getAvatarStyle('default')` returns `height`/`width`/`borderRadius` for the normal avatar size, and `styles.overflowHidden` covers the clipping.

Replace the inline object with the shared helpers, e.g.:
```tsx
const StyleUtils = useStyleUtils();
const styles = useThemeStyles();
// ...
<View style={[StyleUtils.getAvatarStyle(CONST.AVATAR_SIZE.DEFAULT), styles.overflowHidden]}>
```
(Add a small `styles`/`StyleUtils` entry if an exact match is missing, rather than inlining static values.)

This `View` passes an inline style object literal `{backgroundColor: colors.blue800, height: CONST.CONFIRM_CONTENT_SVG_SIZE.HEIGHT}` inside the style array. Inline style objects create a new object on every render (breaking memoization), bypass theming (importing `colors` directly instead of going through the theme), and duplicate values that belong in the style system.

Move these static values into the shared `styles`/`StyleUtils` helpers and reference them from the array instead of inlining the object:

```tsx
// in styles/StyleUtils
trialReminderIllustrationContainer: {
    backgroundColor: theme.blue800,
    height: CONST.CONFIRM_CONTENT_SVG_SIZE.HEIGHT,
},

// usage
<View style={[styles.alignItemsCenter, styles.wAuto, styles.trialReminderIllustrationContainer, styles.pb7]}>
```

This passes an inline object literal `{flexBasis: '48.5%', maxWidth: '48.5%'}` to the `style` prop. Inline style objects are not allowed per `STYLING.md`: they allocate a new object on every render (breaking memoization), bypass the shared style system, and duplicate values that belong in `styles`/`StyleUtils`. The codebase already keeps `flexBasis` styles in the style system (see `src/styles/utils/flex.ts` and `src/styles/index.ts`, e.g. `flexBasis100`, `homePageLeftColumn`). These are static values, so the exception for genuinely dynamic dimensions does not apply.

Move the values into a named style. For example, add a `styles.onboardingAccountingItemWide` entry (or a `StyleUtils` helper) and reference it:

```tsx
// in src/styles/index.ts
onboardingAccountingItemWide: {
    // 48.5% handles the gap between columns and keeps items aligned when the scrollbar appears
    flexBasis: '48.5%',
    maxWidth: '48.5%',
},

// in BaseOnboardingAccounting.tsx
style={[
    styles.onboardingAccountingItem,
    isSmallScreenWidth ? styles.flexBasis100 : styles.onboardingAccountingItemWide,
]}
```

Inline style object literals are not allowed. `{maxHeight: variables.agentRulePromptInputHeight}` is a static value that creates a new object on every render (breaking memoization) and bypasses the shared style system. Since the value is a fixed constant, it belongs in the `styles` system rather than being inlined here.

Add a named style to the shared stylesheet and reference it (this is the same inline style duplicated from `AddAgentRulePage.tsx`, so a single shared style covers both):

```tsx
// in styles
agentRulePromptInput: {
    maxHeight: variables.agentRulePromptInputHeight,
},

// here
const inputWrapperStyles: StyleProp<ViewStyle> = shouldUseExpandedRevampFormLayout
    ? [styles.flex1, styles.mnh0, styles.agentRulePromptInput]
    : [styles.flex1, shouldUseScrollableLayout && styles.minHeight42];
```

Inline style object literals are not allowed. `{maxHeight: variables.agentRulePromptInputHeight}` is a static value that creates a new object on every render (breaking memoization) and bypasses the shared style system. Since the value is a fixed constant, it belongs in the `styles` system rather than being inlined here.

Add a named style to the shared stylesheet and reference it instead:

```tsx
// in styles
agentRulePromptInput: {
    maxHeight: variables.agentRulePromptInputHeight,
},

// here
const inputWrapperStyles: StyleProp<ViewStyle> = shouldUseExpandedRevampFormLayout
    ? [styles.flex1, styles.mnh0, styles.agentRulePromptInput]
    : [styles.flex1, shouldUseScrollableLayout && styles.minHeight42];
```

The pagination-dots container passes an inline object literal `{bottom: PAGINATION_DOTS_BOTTOM_OFFSET + CONTENT_PADDING}` to the `style` array. The value is derived only from static module constants and belongs in the style system; the inline object also allocates a new object on every render.

Extract this into a `StyleUtils` helper or a shared style so it isn't recreated inline, e.g.:

```tsx
// in StyleUtils
getFeatureTrainingCarouselDotsContainerStyle: (): ViewStyle => ({bottom: PAGINATION_DOTS_BOTTOM_OFFSET + CONTENT_PADDING}),

// usage
style={[styles.pAbsolute, styles.flexRow, styles.justifyContentCenter, styles.w100, styles.l0, styles.r0, StyleUtils.getFeatureTrainingCarouselDotsContainerStyle()]}
```

`style={[styles.pAbsolute, {top: CONTENT_PADDING, right: CONTENT_PADDING, zIndex: 1}]}` passes an inline object literal to a style prop. These values are static and belong in the style system; the inline object also creates a new object on every render, defeating memoization and bypassing theming.

Move the static positioning into the shared style sheet (or a `StyleUtils` helper) and reference it instead, e.g.:

```tsx
// in styles
featureTrainingCarouselCloseButton: {
    position: 'absolute',
    top: variables.spacing2,
    right: variables.spacing2,
    zIndex: 1,
},

// usage
<View style={styles.featureTrainingCarouselCloseButton}>
```
